1. Lab Custody Reservation (Forensic Examiner)

As a Forensic Examiner,
I want to reserve a dedicated lab time slot for a piece of evidence,
so that I can prevent double-booking and ensure no other examiner tampers with or analyzes the physical device at the same time.

Acceptance Criteria:
System checks existing bookings and rejects overlapping time slots with an error.
System updates evidence status to RESERVED and logs the checkout when analysis begins.

2. Trial Exhibit Binder & Bates Stamping (Attorney)

As an Attorney,
I want to bundle evidence items into an official Exhibit Binder with sequential Bates page numbers,
so that all exhibits are clearly indexed and legally ready for presentation to the judge and jury.

Acceptance Criteria:
System calculates consecutive Bates numbers automatically (e.g., DEF-01-0001 to DEF-01-0020).
Once the binder is finalized or served, the system locks it against any further modifications.

3. Secure Discovery Production (Opposing Counsel Link)

As an Attorney,
I want to generate a secure, expiring download link for an exhibit binder,
so that I can legally share discovery documents with opposing counsel without having to create an internal login account for them.

Acceptance Criteria:
External lawyer accesses the package using a high-entropy UUID token.
System records their IP address and timestamp as legal Proof of Service.